    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d649">

                <pb facs="0621" n="1355" sameAs="frus:frus1895p2/pg1355"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Olney to Mr.
                            Terrell.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-11-27"><hi rendition="#italic">November 27,
                        1895</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 685.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In view of the sentence from your telegram
                    of the 19th instant, asking, “If you can spare another, send a vessel to Smyrna,
                    to go thence <pb facs="0622" n="1356" xml:id="pg1356"/> wherever needed,” which
                    I quoted to the Secretary of the Navy on the 20th instant, I have now to apprise
                    you of the receipt of Mr. Herbert’s reply of the 23d, observing that the U. S.
                    S. <hi rendition="#italic">Minneapolis</hi> should sail for Smyrna on the 27th
                    instant, and that, allowing for delay of three days at Gibraltar for coal, this
                    vessel should reach her destination on or about the 14th proximo.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Richard Olney.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
